    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"The IMF tools and a reproducible pipeline\"\nsubtitle: \"PEFA Converter, I2A, and the same logic in open code\"\nauthor:\n  - name: Renato Vargas\n  - name: Achille Pegoue\ndate: \"2026-12-07\"\ndate-format: long\nlang: en-US\nbibliography: ../../../assets/references.bib\ncsl: ../../../assets/apa-en.csl\nexecute:\n  echo: false\n  warning: false\nformat:\n  revealjs:\n    theme: [simple, ../../../assets/slides.scss]\n    footer: \"Energy and emissions accounts for Tunisia\"\n    slide-number: true\n    width: 1100\n    height: 700\n    title-slide-attributes:\n      class: theme-title\n      data-state: sans-pied\n---\n\n\n## Two IMF tools {.theme-content}\n\n:::: {.columns}\n::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n**PEFA Converter**\n\nAn Excel workbook with a Python function, `EB2PEFA`, that turns an energy balance in IEA format into physical supply and use tables, through a concordance matrix [@imf2024pefa; @pegoue2026pefa].\n:::\n::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n**Air Emissions Account Converter (I2A)**\n\nAn Excel workbook with a Python function, `I2A`, that turns a greenhouse gas inventory into air emissions accounts by activity, with a residence adjustment from OECD data [@imf2026i2a; @pegoue2026i2a].\n:::\n::::\n\n## How the tools work\n\n```{mermaid}\nflowchart LR\n  EB[\"Energy balance<br/>(IEA layout, TJ)\"] --> CM{{\"Concordance matrix<br/>flow × product → activity\"}}\n  CM --> PSUT[\"Supply and use<br/>tables (PJ)\"]\n  INV[\"Inventory<br/>(CRT, kt CO2 eq)\"] --> CVM{{\"Conversion matrix<br/>category → activity\"}}\n  OECD[\"OECD transport<br/>emissions\"] --> CVM\n  CVM --> AEA[\"Accounts and<br/>bridge table\"]\n```\n\n## From workbook to pipeline\n\n- The same steps, written as **numbered Python scripts** that anyone can read and run.\n- Every allocation choice is a **lookup table** with its reason, not a hidden cell.\n- The scripts call the tool functions **unchanged** and stop if their own result differs:\n  - PEFA: largest gap 5e\\-13 PJ;\n  - AEA: largest gap 7e\\-12 kt CO2 eq.\n- One command compiles everything: `uv run python scripts/run_pipeline.py`.\n\n## The pipeline\n\n| Stage | Scripts | What it does |\n|:--|:--|:--|\n| Extract | 01 to 03 | Read the balance, the inventory and the supply and use tables |\n| PEFA | 10 to 15 | IEA template, keys, concordance matrix, tables, checks, Excel |\n| AEA | 20 to 24 | Inventory, conversion matrix, accounts, bridge, Excel |\n| Report | 30 | Tables and labels for documents and the data explorer |\n\nThe pipeline runs in under a minute; the documents only read its outputs.\n\n## Checks at every step\n\n::: {#4777fd57 .cell execution_count=2}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"hmoevufuii\" style=\"padding-left:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-top:10px;padding-bottom:10px;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:auto;width:auto;height:auto;\">\n<style>\n#hmoevufuii table {\n          font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Fira Sans', 'Droid Sans', Arial, sans-serif;\n          -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n          -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;\n        }\n\n#hmoevufuii thead, #hmoevufuii tbody, #hmoevufuii tfoot, #hmoevufuii tr, #hmoevufuii td, #hmoevufuii th { border-style: none; }\n#hmoevufuii tr { background-color: transparent; }\n#hmoevufuii p { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n #hmoevufuii .gt_table { display: table; border-collapse: collapse; line-height: normal; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; color: #333333; font-size: 18px; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; background-color: #FFFFFF; width: auto; border-top-style: solid; border-top-width: 2px; border-top-color: #204B92; border-right-style: none; border-right-width: 2px; border-right-color: #D3D3D3; border-bottom-style: solid; border-bottom-width: 2px; border-bottom-color: #A8A8A8; border-left-style: none; border-left-width: 2px; border-left-color: #D3D3D3; }\n #hm